Here is the complete, copy-paste-ready Remotion (React + TypeScript) project for the silent, 20-second TechStack Sydney homepage animation (1920×1080, 30fps, 600 frames).
Architecture Highlights
Pure #FFFFFF background & right-half layout: Every illustration, character, laptop, prop, and spark is constrained to x ≥ 995 on the 1920×1080 canvas, leaving the entire left half (x: 0–960) completely clear for captions.
Open Doodles visual language: Loose navy linework (#172047), rounded caps/joins, playful proportions, flat fills strictly in navy, violet (#8B5CF6), and indigo (#3B42B8), subtle doodle motion ticks, and one small multicoloured spark at launch. Zero text, letters, numbers, logos, borders, or player controls.
Single-source character rigs (src/characters/): Owner.tsx and Teammate.tsx share locked proportions, facial features, hair silhouettes, and sweatshirt designs across every cut, driven via rigged <g> transforms.
Exact match cuts & deterministic math: Shared geometry constants (MATCH_CARD and CLOSEUP_SCREEN) ensure pixel-accurate match cuts at 12s and 16s, and all motion uses useCurrentFrame(), spring(), and clamped interpolate().
